<!--
  Synthetic C-CDA Allergies section. No patient data.

  The narrative table is ordered Active Allergy, Reactions, Criticality, Noted
  Date, Comments, so reading it by position (substance, reaction, severity)
  stores the criticality as the severity. Each Allergy - Intolerance
  Observation sits in its own Allergy Concern Act:

    alg-display     drug allergy to an RxNorm-coded substance; an "active"
                    status observation; high criticality; two reactions, the
                    first with a moderate severity
    alg-original    food allergy whose SNOMED substance code's originalText
                    references the narrative cell; a severe severity on the
                    allergy itself; low criticality; the concern is completed,
                    which is not the allergy's status (still active)
    alg-name        environmental allergy to a substance with only a <name>;
                    it has ended
    alg-inactive    "allergy to substance" (no category); an "inactive" status
                    observation; criticality unable to assess
    alg-code-only   nothing but the RxNorm code names the substance
    alg-nka         negationInd with no substance: no known allergies
    alg-unnamed     nothing names the substance, and its text references its
                    own row

  Every observation but alg-original, alg-code-only and alg-nka references its
  row through its text; alg-original references it through its substance.
-->
